if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-2-database-apis-8' and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('A team believes that adopting JDBC alone eliminates the need to think about drivers, middleware, or connection pooling ever again. Why does this misunderstand the layered stack described?','["It is correct; JDBC alone handles every concern in the stack automatically", "JDBC (the API) only standardizes the calling contract; the driver still does vendor translation, and middleware/pooling still separately manage routing and connection reuse \u2014 these are distinct layers with distinct responsibilities", "Drivers and middleware are optional add-ons with no real function", "Connection pooling is part of the JDBC standard itself and requires no separate configuration"]'::jsonb,1,'The API, driver, and middleware/pooling layers each solve a different problem (what to call, how it''s translated, and when/through which connection) — adopting a standard API does not subsume the responsibilities of the other layers.') and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('A team believes that adopting JDBC alone eliminates the need to think about drivers, middleware, or connection pooling ever again. Why does this misunderstand the layered stack described?','["It is correct; JDBC alone handles every concern in the stack automatically", "JDBC (the API) only standardizes the calling contract; the driver still does vendor translation, and middleware/pooling still separately manage routing and connection reuse \u2014 these are distinct layers with distinct responsibilities", "Drivers and middleware are optional add-ons with no real function", "Connection pooling is part of the JDBC standard itself and requires no separate configuration"]'::jsonb,1,'The API, driver, and middleware/pooling layers each solve a different problem (what to call, how it''s translated, and when/through which connection) — adopti