(1, ''Asha'', ''Engineering'', 85000, NULL),
(2, ''Rohan'', ''Engineering'', 72000, 1),
(3, ''Neha'', ''Sales'', 68000, NULL),
(4, ''Vikram'', ''Sales'', 61000, 3),
(5, ''Priya'', ''Engineering'', 79000, 1),
(6, ''Karan'', ''Marketing'', 55000, NULL),
(7, ''Divya'', ''Marketing'', 58000, 6),
(8, ''Aman'', ''Sales'', 64000, 3);
```

**Required ordering:** salary descending, id ascending

**Edge cases:**
- Equal sort values require the stated tie-breaker
- An empty input returns no rows
- Only the intended department population contributes','[{"input": "INSERT INTO employees (id, name, department, salary, manager_id) VALUES\n(1, ''Asha'', ''Engineering'', 85000, NULL),\n(2, ''Rohan'', ''Engineering'', 72000, 1),\n(3, ''Neha'', ''Sales'', 68000, NULL),\n(4, ''Vikram'', ''Sales'', 61000, 3),\n(5, ''Priya'', ''Engineering'', 79000, 1),\n(6, ''Karan'', ''Marketing'', 55000, NULL),\n(7, ''Divya'', ''Marketing'', 58000, 6),\n(8, ''Aman'', ''Sales'', 64000, 3);", "output": "id\tname\tsalary\n1\tAsha\t85000\n5\tPriya\t79000\n2\tRohan\t72000", "explanation": "The explicit projection and department predicate preserve the retained listing task. Salary rank and identifier tie-breaker make its sequence deterministic."}]'::jsonb,'[{"seed_sql": "INSERT INTO employees (id, name, department, salary, manager_id) VALUES\n(1, ''Zara'', ''Engineering'', 90000, NULL),\n(2, ''Omar'', ''Engineering'', 90000, 1),\n(3, ''Leo'', ''Finance'', 70000, NULL),\n(4, ''Mia'', ''Finance'', 66000, 3),\n(5, ''Sam'', ''Engineering'', 58000, 1),\n(6, ''Tia'', ''Finance'', 72000, 3);", "expected": "id\tname\tsalary\n1\tZara\t90000\n2\tOmar\t90000\n5\tSam\t58000", "hidden": true}, {"seed_sql": "", "expected": "", "hidden": true}]'::jsonb,'["Existing employee IDs, schema, and setup retained", "Salary is a required integer", "Names can repeat"]'::jsonb,'["Use a department row filter", "Request both ordering keys"]'::jsonb,'{"sql": "-- Write your SELECT query here\n"}'::jsonb,'The explicit projection and department predicate preserve the retained listing task. Salary rank and identifier tie-breaker make its sequence deterministic.','{"sql": "SELECT id,name,salary FROM employees WHERE department = ''Engineering'' ORDER BY salary DESC,id ASC;"}'::jsonb,'The explicit projection and department predicate preserve the retained listing task. Salary rank and identifier tie-breaker make its sequence deterministic.',array['sql'],'CREATE TABLE employees (
