Users also contribute to reliable operation by following the intended process and reporting unexpected outcomes. However, the application must not rely on every user avoiding every malformed request or remembering an undocumented rule. The designer and developer should make required information and permitted actions clear, while trusted enforcement handles requests that do not follow the intended screen flow.

## Seeing the work of designers, developers, and operators

The database designer helps define what the system''s records and relationships mean. The application developer turns those definitions into workflows and responses. The database administrator or assigned operator helps keep the deployed service available, recoverable, and appropriately controlled. An end user may encounter these roles indirectly through the service, but that does not mean the operator is always invisible or can never communicate with users.

For example, an outage notice may be coordinated by operations staff, while a confusing form may require developer and user-experience work. An incorrect assumption about repeated assessments may require design review. A useful issue report describes the task, the observed outcome, and the relevant nonprivate context. It should not require the user to diagnose an index or invent a database explanation for the symptom.

These responsibilities can overlap in a small team, yet they remain worth distinguishing. The person operating the database may also write the interface. That does not mean the user''s everyday request should execute with all of that person''s administrative privileges. The implementation must preserve the boundary appropriate to the user task rather than expose every capability the team possesses.

## Reviewing whether the interaction fits its purpose

Evaluate a routine workflow with concrete cases. Can the student find the intended assessment using keyboard controls? Is the result labeled clearly? What happens when no result is available? Does invalid input lead to an understandable response? Is a denied attempt handled according to the access contract? Can the user tell a failed update from a completed one? These checks examine the actual interaction rather than only its visual appearance.

For flexible reporting, ask whether the authorized user can answer the required questions and whether the tool prevents access beyond the approved scope. A useful system may combine fixed forms with controlled reporting facilities. There is no requirement that every participant use the same interface merely because they share a database.

The end-user perspective therefore provides an important test of the whole design. Stored data and sophisticated infrastructure are useful only when the permitted person can complete the intended task reliably. Keep the interface understandable, the outcomes truthful, and the enforcement boundaries intact. That supports both routine users who never need SQL and authorized specialists whose work benefits from more flexible data access.' or heading is distinct from 'End User');
update public.learning_topics set short_description='Understand end users as task-specific participants, from fixed forms to flexible reporting, with clear states, truthful outcomes, and trusted record-level access boundaries.',updated_at=now() where id=topic_uuid and short_description is distinct from 'Understand end users as task-specific participants, from fixed forms to flexible reporting, with clear states, truthful outcomes, and trusted record-level access boundaries.';
update public.practice_tests set title='MCQ Test 1',question_count=10,total_marks=10,pass_marks=4,duration_minutes=10,description='Concepts and fundamentals for End User.',instructions='Answer all ten questions. One mark each; no negative marking.',updated_at=now() where id='pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user' and (title<>'MCQ Test 1' or question_count<>10 or total_marks<>10);
insert into public.practice_tests (id,title,category,question_count,duration_minutes,description,total_marks,pass_marks,is_published,difficulty,learning_grid_id,learning_topic_id,status,is_premium,negative_marking,instructions,show_on_website,show_on_mobile,scope) select 'pt-dbx2-end-user-application','MCQ Test 2',category,10,10,'Application and scenarios for End User.',10,4,is_published,difficulty,learning_grid_id,learning_topic_id,status,is_premium,0,'Answer all ten questions. One mark each; no negative marking.',show_on_website,show_on_mobile,'topic' from public.practice_tests where id='pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user' on conflict(id) do nothing;
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbms-sql-1-end-user-1','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','What defines the routine application end user in this topic''s examples?','["Someone who interacts with the database only through an application''s interface, without needing to know SQL or the schema", "Someone who designs the ER diagram for a new system", "Someone who manages backups and performance tuning", "Someone who writes the application''s business logic code"]'::jsonb,0,'The notes define the End User as consuming data through an application interface without needing SQL, schema, or DBMS-internals knowledge.',1,0) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbms-sql-1-end-user-2','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','What is the difference between a naive end user and a sophisticated/casual end user, per the notes?','["A naive user interacts purely through fixed forms, while a sophisticated/casual user may use reporting or BI tools for more flexible queries", "A naive user has full DBA privileges, while a sophisticated user has none", "There is no difference; the terms are interchangeable", "A sophisticated end user is always also the Database Designer"]'::jsonb,0,'The notes explicitly distinguish naive end users (fixed forms) from casual/sophisticated end users (flexible reporting/BI tools).',1,1) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbms-sql-1-end-user-3','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','In the student portal example, what does the End User see when checking their grades?','["Their attendance percentage and marks through buttons and forms, without seeing table names or SQL", "The raw SQL JOIN query used to fetch their data", "The database''s system catalog metadata", "A direct connection prompt to the DBMS server"]'::jsonb,0,'The notes describe the End User''s experience as buttons and forms only, with no visibility into tables, JOINs, or indexes.',1,2) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbms-sql-1-end-user-4','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','How do developer and DBA responsibilities contribute differently to ordinary portal use?','["The developer shapes the task interface and implementation; the DBA helps operate and control the deployed service", "A DBA can never communicate with a user", "The developer automatically owns every user''s records", "The DBA''s duties disappear once a form exists"]'::jsonb,0,'Operations commonly work behind the interface but are not inherently invisible. These are complementary responsibilities, not a rule about who may communicate with users.',1,3) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbms-sql-1-end-user-5','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','Why does the notes say ''End User'' describes a role in a specific interaction rather than a permanent skill level?','["Because the same person can be a Developer on one project and simply an End User of a completely different, unrelated system", "Because every End User eventually becomes a DBA over time", "Because the term only applies to students, never to staff", "Because End Users are legally required to rotate roles annually"]'::jsonb,0,'The notes explicitly make this point: the same individual can occupy different roles depending on which system they are interacting with.',1,4) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbms-sql-1-end-user-6','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','What should happen when a student requests another student''s restricted grades?','["The trusted server or database access boundary must reject the unauthorized request", "Changing an identifier grants access automatically", "Hiding a button alone is sufficient authorization", "Every student must have administrative database privileges"]'::jsonb,0,'The actual actor and requested records must be checked at the trusted boundary, including requests that bypass the intended interface.',1,5) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbms-sql-1-end-user-7','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','A college gives a non-technical exam clerk a raw SQL query screen instead of a guided form. What does the notes call this?','["A design failure, because it exposes complexity the End User role is meant to be shielded from", "A best practice that should be applied to all end users", "An example of correctly classifying a sophisticated end user", "A necessary step required by the DBMS Goals topic"]'::jsonb,0,'The notes explicitly label giving raw SQL access to a naive end user as a design failure that violates the intended usability contract.',1,6) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbms-sql-1-end-user-8','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','A data analyst who is a genuinely sophisticated end user is restricted to only a handful of canned, pre-built reports with no ad-hoc query capability. What does the notes say about this situation?','["It can be an operational bottleneck, since access should be matched to real need rather than arbitrarily minimized", "It is always correct, since all end users must be restricted to canned reports", "It has no downside because sophisticated end users never need flexible reporting", "It violates the DBMS''s crash recovery guarantees"]'::jsonb,0,'The notes explicitly warn that over-restricting a genuinely sophisticated end user can be a bottleneck to legitimate work.',1,7) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-1-9','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','Does an end-user role permanently describe a person''s technical skill?','["Yes; developers can never be end users", "No; it describes the interaction with this system and task", "Yes; every end user is unable to understand data", "No; every interaction must expose a schema"]'::jsonb,1,'A technically experienced person can be a routine user of another application.',1,8) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-1-10','pt-dbms-sql-1-end-user','What should a form confirmation communicate?','["That a button was clicked, regardless of failure", "A fabricated successful update", "The actual confirmed outcome of the requested operation", "Every private diagnostic detail"]'::jsonb,2,'Users need to distinguish a completed operation from a failed or unconfirmed request.',1,9) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-1','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','A database developer checks a ticket booking through a normal application. Which role can they be performing?','["Automatically the booking system''s DBA", "Every administrative role at once", "An end-user role for that interaction", "No role, because they know SQL"]'::jsonb,2,'Professional expertise does not remove the person''s role as a user of the booking service.',1,0) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-2','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','A teacher sees an assessment score without its assessment name. What usability risk arises?','["The value can be interpreted as belonging to the wrong assessment", "The missing label grants schema privileges", "The database must have deleted every record", "The value automatically becomes current for every task"]'::jsonb,0,'A result needs enough verified context to support correct interpretation.',1,1) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-3','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','A clerk needs a narrowly defined approved correction workflow. Which interface is ordinarily appropriate?','["A guided form with suitable validation and trusted enforcement", "An unrestricted SQL console by default", "A rule granting every clerk schema ownership", "Only a photograph of a table"]'::jsonb,0,'The interface should support the permitted task and avoid unnecessary operational complexity.',1,2) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-4','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','An authorized analyst cannot answer required questions using the available canned reports. What should be evaluated?','["Automatic unrestricted access to every private record", "A scoped flexible reporting path matching the legitimate need", "A permanent ban on all additional reports", "Whether SQL skill implies administration authority"]'::jsonb,1,'Useful flexibility and restricted access can coexist when the reporting path is deliberately designed.',1,3) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-5','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','A results query fails, but the screen says there are no marks. What has been confused?','["A permission grant with a font choice", "Service failure with a genuine empty result", "A primary key with an index name", "A successful update with a table definition"]'::jsonb,1,'The user needs a truthful state appropriate to the operation, not an empty result that hides a failure.',1,4) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-6','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','A student modifies a request to ask for another student''s private marks. What must happen?','["The hidden button alone guarantees rejection", "The changed identifier grants ownership", "The trusted access boundary rejects the unauthorized operation", "The system must expose the other student''s record existence"]'::jsonb,2,'Authorization must evaluate the real request, actor and record, according to the relevant response contract.',1,5) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-7','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','A user can read their own marks. What does this not imply?','["That an authorized view can exist", "Permission to change those marks", "That records may have identifiers", "That a result can be labeled"]'::jsonb,1,'Read and update are separate operations and may require different authority.',1,6) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-8','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','An error response deliberately avoids confirming whether a private record exists. Should the interface expose the internal record anyway?','["No; it must respect the access and disclosure contract", "Yes; every internal diagnostic belongs in the response", "Yes; an unavailable screen revokes all privacy rules", "No; it should always fabricate success instead"]'::jsonb,0,'Limited disclosure can be intentional. Diagnostics should follow the appropriate authorized path.',1,7) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-9','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','A user reports that a form failed. What is useful for them to supply?','["Private credentials copied into a public message", "A guessed index change to run in production", "An assumption that every failure has the same database cause", "The task and observed outcome with relevant nonprivate context"]'::jsonb,3,'Users can report observable behavior without being required to diagnose internal database machinery.',1,8) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
insert into public.test_questions (id,test_id,question_text,options,correct_index,explanation,marks,sort_order) values ('tq-dbx2-end-user-2-10','pt-dbx2-end-user-application','A shared system offers both fixed forms and approved reporting. Is that inherently inconsistent?','["Yes; every user must receive identical controls", "Yes; reporting users must become administrators", "No; flexible reporting removes access restrictions", "No; different authorized tasks can need different interaction styles"]'::jsonb,3,'The interface should match task needs while the trusted boundaries preserve the correct authority.',1,9) on conflict(id) do update set question_text=excluded.question_text,options=excluded.options,correct_index=excluded.correct_index,explanation=excluded.explanation where (test_questions.question_text,test_questions.options,test_questions.correct_index,test_questions.explanation) is distinct from (excluded.question_text,excluded.options,excluded.correct_index,excluded.explanation);
-- entity-integrity
select t.id into strict topic_uuid from public.learning_topics t join public.learning_grids g on g.id=t.grid_id where t.source_kind='dbms_sql_tutorial' and t.source_ref='chapter-5-keys-and-integrity/entity-integrity' and lower(g.slug)='dbms-sql-tutorial';
if (select count(*) from public.learning_contents c where c.topic_id=topic_uuid and c.metadata->>'source'='dbms_sql_tutorial_seed') <> 1 then raise exception 'Expected one canonical note block: %', 'entity-integrity'; end if;
if (select count(*) from public.learning_contents c where c.topic_id=topic_uuid) <> 1 then raise exception 'Additional content blocks require review: %', 'entity-integrity'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.learning_contents c where c.topic_id=topic_uuid and c.metadata->>'source'='dbms_sql_tutorial_seed' and md5(c.body) not in ('975caef6facecb5a56d9468835b5716d','e87b67890138d798ecc2afe247d6328d')) then raise exception 'Notes changed since seed; review before applying: %', 'entity-integrity'; end if;
if not exists(select 1 from public.practice_tests where id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity' and learning_topic_id=topic_uuid and scope='topic') then raise exception 'Missing original topic test: %', 'entity-integrity'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.practice_tests where id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity' and coalesce(negative_marking,0)<>0) then raise exception 'Custom scoring requires review: %', 'entity-integrity'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.practice_tests where learning_topic_id=topic_uuid and scope='topic' and id not in ('pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity','pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-application')) then raise exception 'Extra topic tests require manual integration: %', 'entity-integrity'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.practice_tests where id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-application' and learning_topic_id is distinct from topic_uuid) then raise exception 'Test ID collision: %', 'entity-integrity'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.learning_contents where topic_id=topic_uuid and metadata->'dbms_diagrams_v1' is not null and metadata->'dbms_diagrams_v1' is distinct from '[{"kind": "table", "caption": "Identity rules and non-key data rules answer different questions", "description": "The designated identifier must remain unique and nonmissing. Repeated names and permitted absent scores do not violate that identity contract.", "columns": ["Proposed change", "Entity-identity result", "Separate issue"], "rows": [["New id, repeated name", "Permitted by primary identity", "Check other applicable rules"], ["Existing id, different name", "Reject duplicate identity", "Name difference does not create a new student id"], ["Missing id", "Reject incomplete primary identity", "Generation is excluded in these fixtures"], ["New id, missing optional score", "Permitted by primary identity", "Score absence follows its own policy"]]}]'::jsonb) then raise exception 'Edited diagram metadata requires review: %', 'entity-integrity'; end if;
update public.learning_contents set metadata=jsonb_set(coalesce(metadata,'{}'::jsonb),'{dbms_diagrams_v1}','[{"kind": "table", "caption": "Identity rules and non-key data rules answer different questions", "description": "The designated identifier must remain unique and nonmissing. Repeated names and permitted absent scores do not violate that identity contract.", "columns": ["Proposed change", "Entity-identity result", "Separate issue"], "rows": [["New id, repeated name", "Permitted by primary identity", "Check other applicable rules"], ["Existing id, different name", "Reject duplicate identity", "Name difference does not create a new student id"], ["Missing id", "Reject incomplete primary identity", "Generation is excluded in these fixtures"], ["New id, missing optional score", "Permitted by primary identity", "Score absence follows its own policy"]]}]'::jsonb),updated_at=now() where topic_id=topic_uuid and metadata->>'source'='dbms_sql_tutorial_seed' and metadata->'dbms_diagrams_v1' is distinct from '[{"kind": "table", "caption": "Identity rules and non-key data rules answer different questions", "description": "The designated identifier must remain unique and nonmissing. Repeated names and permitted absent scores do not violate that identity contract.", "columns": ["Proposed change", "Entity-identity result", "Separate issue"], "rows": [["New id, repeated name", "Permitted by primary identity", "Check other applicable rules"], ["Existing id, different name", "Reject duplicate identity", "Name difference does not create a new student id"], ["Missing id", "Reject incomplete primary identity", "Generation is excluded in these fixtures"], ["New id, missing optional score", "Permitted by primary identity", "Score absence follows its own policy"]]}]'::jsonb;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity' and id not in ('tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-1','tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-2','tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-3','tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-4','tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-5','tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-6','tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-7','tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-8','pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-new-9','pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-new-10')) then raise exception 'Unexpected questions require review: %', 'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity' and marks<>1) then raise exception 'Custom question marks require review: %', 'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-1' and test_id<>'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Question ID collision: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-1'; end if;
if not exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-1' and test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Original question was removed; review required: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-1'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-1' and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('What does entity integrity guarantee?','["That every column value is unique", "That the primary key is always unique and never NULL", "That every table has at least 10 rows", "That foreign keys always match a parent row"]'::jsonb,1,'Entity integrity is specifically about the primary key''s uniqueness and non-nullability.') and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('What does entity integrity guarantee?','["That every column value is unique", "That the primary key is always unique and never NULL", "That every table has at least 10 rows", "That foreign keys always match a parent row"]'::jsonb,1,'Entity integrity is specifically about the primary key''s uniqueness and non-nullability.')) then raise exception 'Edited question requires review: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-1'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-2' and test_id<>'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Question ID collision: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-2'; end if;
if not exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-2' and test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Original question was removed; review required: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-2'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-2' and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('How is entity integrity enforced in SQL?','["By writing a custom trigger for every table", "Automatically, simply by declaring a column PRIMARY KEY", "By adding a CHECK constraint manually", "Entity integrity cannot be enforced by SQL"]'::jsonb,1,'PRIMARY KEY bundles both the uniqueness and NOT NULL requirements automatically.') and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('How is entity integrity enforced in SQL?','["By writing a custom trigger for every table", "Through a supported PRIMARY KEY declaration over the chosen identifying attributes", "By adding a CHECK constraint manually", "Entity integrity cannot be enforced by SQL"]'::jsonb,1,'PRIMARY KEY bundles both the uniqueness and NOT NULL requirements automatically.')) then raise exception 'Edited question requires review: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-2'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-3' and test_id<>'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Question ID collision: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-3'; end if;
if not exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-3' and test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Original question was removed; review required: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-3'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-3' and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('Why is a NULL primary key value considered a serious problem?','["It merely wastes a small amount of storage", "It would create a row with no well-defined identity, making it impossible to reliably reference or distinguish from other rows", "NULL values take longer to compare than other values", "It is not actually a problem in modern databases"]'::jsonb,1,'A NULL identity breaks the fundamental guarantee that every row can be uniquely and unambiguously referred to.') and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('Why is a NULL primary key value considered a serious problem?','["It merely wastes a small amount of storage", "It violates the requirement that the designated primary identity be complete and definite", "NULL values take longer to compare than other values", "It is not actually a problem in modern databases"]'::jsonb,1,'The primary identity must be nonmissing. Another identifier may exist, but that does not satisfy the declared primary-key contract.')) then raise exception 'Edited question requires review: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-3'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-4' and test_id<>'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Question ID collision: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-4'; end if;
if not exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-4' and test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Original question was removed; review required: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-4'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-4' and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('Does entity integrity apply to alternate keys enforced via UNIQUE?','["Yes, identically to primary keys", "No \u2014 entity integrity specifically concerns the PRIMARY KEY; a UNIQUE alternate key can still permit NULLs", "Only if the alternate key is also composite", "Entity integrity applies to every column in the table"]'::jsonb,1,'Entity integrity is a primary-key-specific rule; UNIQUE alone doesn''t carry the same NOT-NULL guarantee.') and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('Does entity integrity apply to alternate keys enforced via UNIQUE?','["Yes, identically to primary keys", "The primary-key rule is distinct; a required alternate identity needs its own appropriate uniqueness and nonmissing policy", "Only if the alternate key is also composite", "Entity integrity applies to every column in the table"]'::jsonb,1,'Do not conflate nullable UNIQUE behaviour with a required alternate candidate identity.')) then raise exception 'Edited question requires review: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-4'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-5' and test_id<>'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Question ID collision: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-5'; end if;
if not exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-5' and test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Original question was removed; review required: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-5'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-5' and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('For a composite primary key, what does entity integrity require about its individual component columns?','["Only the first column needs to be NOT NULL", "None of the component columns may be NULL \u2014 a NULL in any part breaks the row''s overall identity guarantee", "At least one component column must be NULL", "Composite keys are exempt from entity integrity"]'::jsonb,1,'Since the full combination defines the row''s identity, every component column must be non-null for that identity to be complete and known.') and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('For a composite primary key, what does entity integrity require about its individual component columns?','["Only the first column needs to be NOT NULL", "None of the component columns may be NULL \u2014 a NULL in any part breaks the row''s overall identity guarantee", "At least one component column must be NULL", "Composite keys are exempt from entity integrity"]'::jsonb,1,'Since the full combination defines the row''s identity, every component column must be non-null for that identity to be complete and known.')) then raise exception 'Edited question requires review: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-5'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-6' and test_id<>'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Question ID collision: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-6'; end if;
if not exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-6' and test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Original question was removed; review required: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-6'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-6' and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('Does satisfying entity integrity guarantee that a row''s data is otherwise correct?','["Yes, entity integrity guarantees full data correctness", "No \u2014 entity integrity only guarantees the row has a valid, unique, non-null identity; other columns could still contain wrong or nonsensical values", "Entity integrity guarantees correctness only for numeric columns", "This question doesn''t apply to entity integrity"]'::jsonb,1,'Entity integrity is necessary but not sufficient — it says nothing about whether the rest of the row''s data is accurate.') and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('Does satisfying entity integrity guarantee that a row''s data is otherwise correct?','["Yes, entity integrity guarantees full data correctness", "No \u2014 entity integrity only guarantees the row has a valid, unique, non-null identity; other columns could still contain wrong or nonsensical values", "Entity integrity guarantees correctness only for numeric columns", "This question doesn''t apply to entity integrity"]'::jsonb,1,'Entity integrity is necessary but not sufficient — it says nothing about whether the rest of the row''s data is accurate.')) then raise exception 'Edited question requires review: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-6'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-7' and test_id<>'pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Question ID collision: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-7'; end if;
if not exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-7' and test_id='pt-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity') then raise exception 'Original question was removed; review required: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-7'; end if;
if exists(select 1 from public.test_questions where id='tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-7' and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('What real ambiguity would arise from two rows both having primary key value 7?','["No ambiguity \u2014 the database would simply pick one at random consistently", "Any query or foreign key referencing ''the row with id 7'' would have no way to know which of the two rows was meant", "SQL would automatically rename one of the rows", "This scenario is impossible to describe in relational terms, but has no practical consequence"]'::jsonb,1,'Duplicate primary key values destroy the ability to unambiguously reference a specific row, which is exactly what entity integrity prevents.') and (question_text,options,correct_index,explanation) is distinct from ('What real ambiguity would arise from two rows both having primary key value 7?','["No ambiguity \u2014 the database would simply pick one at random consistently", "Any query or foreign key referencing ''the row with id 7'' would have no way to know which of the two rows was meant", "SQL would automatically rename one of the rows", "This scenario is impossible to describe in relational terms, but has no practical consequence"]'::jsonb,1,'Duplicate primary key values destroy the ability to unambiguously reference a specific row, which is exactly what entity integrity prevents.')) then raise exception 'Edited question requires review: %', 'tq-dbms-sql-5-entity-integrity-7'; end if;
