insert into public.dsa_problems (id,topic_id,title,difficulty,slug,description,examples,test_cases,constraints,hints,starter_code,editorial,solution_code,solution_approach,supported_languages,sql_schema_sql,sql_seed_sql,learning_topic_id,status,is_premium,show_on_website,show_on_mobile,sort_order) select 'cp-dbms-sql-copy-high-performers',null::text,'Copy High Performers','Medium','copy-high-performers','Copy each employee with salary>=80000 into initially empty high_performers, mapping id,name,salary explicitly. Preserve source employees. Submit the write only; the retained trailing checker reads the destination in id order. This is a one-time copy, not an automatic idempotent retry policy.

**MySQL dialect.**

```sql
CREATE TABLE employees (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, salary INTEGER NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE high_performers (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, salary INTEGER NOT NULL);
INSERT INTO employees (id, name, salary) VALUES
(1, ''Asha'', 85000), (2, ''Rohan'', 62000), (3, ''Neha'', 91000);
```

**Required ordering:** The original checker orders destination rows by id.

**Edge cases:**
- Salary exactly 80000 qualifies.
