if exists(select 1 from public.dsa_problems where id='cx-unique-optional-code' and description is distinct from 'Add UNIQUE(badge_code) named badge_identity to badges. NULL means unassigned and may occur on several rows under the MySQL contract. Return student_id and code_state, the badge_code when present or unassigned when NULL. Do not store the display fallback.

**MySQL dialect.**

```sql
CREATE TABLE badges (student_id INT PRIMARY KEY, badge_code VARCHAR(30) NULL);
INSERT INTO badges VALUES (1,''B1''),(2,''B2''),(3,NULL),(4,NULL);
```

**Required ordering:** Ascending student_id.

**Edge cases:**
- Multiple NULL values remain allowed.
