**MySQL dialect.**

```sql
CREATE TABLE buildings (building_id INT PRIMARY KEY, building_name VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE rooms (building_id INT NOT NULL, room_number INT NOT NULL, capacity INT NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY (building_id, room_number));
INSERT INTO buildings VALUES (7,''North Hall''),(9,''South Hall''),(12,''New Hall''); INSERT INTO rooms VALUES (7,101,30),(7,102,20),(9,101,40);
```

**Required ordering:** Ascending building_id, room_number for listings; a complete identity lookup returns at most one row.

**Edge cases:**
- Different owners can both have Room 101.
- A building can have no rooms.','[{"input": "INSERT INTO buildings VALUES (7,''North Hall''),(9,''South Hall''),(12,''New Hall''); INSERT INTO rooms VALUES (7,101,30),(7,102,20),(9,101,40);", "output": "building_id\troom_count\ttotal_capacity\n7\t2\t50\n9\t1\t40\n12\t0\t0", "explanation": "The query preserves owner-dependent room identity. The fixture\u2019s composite key is real, while foreign-key and parent-action behaviour need separate native checks."}]'::jsonb,'[{"seed_sql": "INSERT INTO buildings VALUES (7,''North Hall''),(9,''South Hall''); INSERT INTO rooms VALUES (7,101,10),(9,101,20);", "expected": "building_id\troom_count\ttotal_capacity\n7\t1\t10\n9\t1\t20", "hidden": true}, {"seed_sql": "INSERT INTO buildings VALUES (12,''New Hall'');", "expected": "building_id\troom_count\ttotal_capacity\n12\t0\t0", "hidden": true}]'::jsonb,'["Room numbers are unique within a building, not across buildings.", "Temporary query mirrors omit foreign keys; native reference enforcement is verified separately when supported."]'::jsonb,'["Carry the owner identity alongside the partial key.", "Join through building_id rather than a descriptive label."]'::jsonb,'{"sql": "-- Write your SELECT query here\n"}'::jsonb,'The query preserves owner-dependent room identity. The fixture’s composite key is real, while foreign-key and parent-action behaviour need separate native checks.','{"sql": "SELECT b.building_id, COUNT(r.room_number) AS room_count, COALESCE(SUM(r.capacity), 0) AS total_capacity FROM buildings b LEFT JOIN rooms r ON r.building_id = b.building_id GROUP BY b.building_id ORDER BY b.building_id;"}'::jsonb,'The query preserves owner-dependent room identity. The fixture’s composite key is real, while foreign-key and parent-action behaviour need separate native checks.',array['sql'],'CREATE TABLE buildings (building_id INT PRIMARY KEY, building_name VARCHAR(80) NOT NULL);
